<title>UK: Dominion says may bid for East Mids.</title>
<headline>Dominion says may bid for East Mids.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dominion Resources Inc said on Wednesday that it may launch a bid for Britain's East Midlands Electricity Plc.</p>
<p>In a statement the U.S. company said it did not intend to offer &quot;much in excess of East Midlands Electricity's closing price today of 608 pence per share&quot;.  </p>
<p>Dominion said its board would meet soon to consider whether to make a bid.</p>
<p>Dominion said it issued the statement in the wake of growing speculation about a possible bid for East Midlands, which saw its shares surge 70-1/2 pence to 608 pence on Wednesday.</p>
<p>No-one at East Midlands Electricity was immediately avaliable for comment.</p>
</text>
